.TH TLSGET 1
.SH NAME
tlsget \- fetch a Gemini URL over TLS 1.3 from Dis
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tlsget
.I host[!port]
.RI [ path
.RI [ servername ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tlsget
dials
.I host
at
.I port
(default 1965), performs a TLS 1.3 client handshake in Dis, requests
.BI gemini:// servername path
and writes the response to standard output.
It prints the SHA-256 fingerprint of the server's leaf certificate
before the response.
.PP
.I Servername
defaults to the host part of the address and is used both as the SNI
name and in the request URL, so a capsule can be reached by address
when name resolution is unavailable.
.PP
The handshake uses
.IR tls (2)
for AES-128-GCM records and ECDSA P-256 verification,
.IR mono (2)
for X25519, and
.IR crypt (2)
for SHA-256.  It accepts
.B TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
with an X25519 key share and an ECDSA P-256 server certificate.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
tlsget tlgs.one
tlsget 142.132.165.255!1965 / tlgs.one
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/tlsget.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR tls (2),
.IR mono (2),
.IR gemserve (8)
.SH BUGS
There is no TLS 1.2 fallback, no Ed25519 or RSA certificate support,
no session resumption, and no certificate pinning: the fingerprint is
reported, not checked.  The response and the fingerprint share standard
output.
